    "/apis/v1/who-int/indicators/dimensions": {
      "post": {
        "operationId": "who-int.indicators.dimensions",
        "summary": "Dimensions",
        "description": "List the values of one GHO dimension (COUNTRY, REGION, WORLDBANKINCOMEGROUP, SEX, AGEGROUP, ...): code, title and parent (countries carry their WHO region). Omit dimension_code to list the dimensions themselves. Unknown dimension codes fail with not_found.",
        "requestBody": {
          "required": false,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "additionalProperties": true,
                "properties": {
                  "dimension_code": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Dimension code from /api/Dimension. Omit or null to list all dimensions. Pattern: ^[A-Za-z0-9_.+-]{1,64}$.",
                    "x-alexandria-option-metadata": {
                      "in": "body"
                    }
                  }
                }
              },
              "examples": {
                "provider": {
                  "summary": "Official provider example; checked against AIsa request constraints",
                  "value": {
                    "dimension_code": "SEX"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "List the values of one GHO dimension (COUNTRY, REGION, WORLDBANKINCOMEGROUP, SEX, AGEGROUP, ...): code, title and parent (countries carry their WHO region). Omit dimension_code to list the dimensions themselves. Unknown dimension codes fail with not_found.\n\nThe response contains the tool result directly.\n\n| Documented field | Provider type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `complete` | boolean |  |\n| `dimension_code` | string |  |\n| `license` | object | Source-defined WHO metadata. |\n| `next_cursor` | object | Dimension value sets are returned whole (largest is COUNTRY, 234 rows). |\n| `records` | object[] |  |\n| `retrieved_at` | string |  |\n| `schema_version` | string |  |\n| `source_updated_at` | object |  |\n| `source_url` | string |  |\n| `total_count` | number |  |\n| `upstream_requests` | number |  |\n| `warnings` | string[] |  |\n\n\nThese are the provider's documented fields. Field requiredness, nullability and nested object structures are specified only where the descriptions explicitly say so.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "not": {
